The Green Father is an entity that resides within the [[Verdant Expanse]]. Little is known about the Green Father, other than that it's believed he encourages the agricultural cultivation of arable lands.

@deity "Green Father"
| category: Inner God
{
Edicts :: Tend to the land, grow new and strange flora
Anathema :: Tear down existing plantlife, disrupt the natural order
[[Divine Raiment]] :: Green, floral
[[Celestial Prescence]] :: Occasional green flares
}

In [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]] a small number of people are devout to the Green Father. They hold him to be the [[Verdant Expanse]] itself rather than a person, and their worship leads them to set aside recent inventions and anything too far from what they see as a natural state. They keep to the [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford Commune|Wrenford commune]]. Their raiments tend toward green, and where the green overtakes the pearlescent the small vines of the raiment begin to wrap around it.

The [[Bestiary/Fey|court of fey]] that holds a glade in the deep forest calls the Green Father "the one that the silly little ones outside worship," and knows of it without following it.
